x ln xaln x + x # 1"},{"x":0.64776,"y":0.41843,"w":0.01664,"h":0.02747,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"xb"},{"x":0.52191,"y":0.45381,"w":0.20841,"h":0.01727,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"= xx (ln x + 1). x 7 0"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.47988,"w":0.58812,"h":0.02957,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"We can also find the derivative of y = xx using logarithmic differentiation, assuming y′ exists."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.53338,"w":0.2735,"h":0.01394,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The Number e Expressed as a Limit"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.55802,"w":0.58902,"h":0.0435,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"In Section 1.5 we defined the number e as the base value for which the exponential func- tion y = ax has slope 1 when it crosses the y-axis at (0, 1). Thus e is the constant that sat- isfies the equation"},{"x":0.47035,"y":0.61475,"w":0.04522,"h":0.01795,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"eh - 1"},{"x":0.48887,"y":0.62642,"w":0.3059,"h":0.02074,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"h = ln e = 1. Slope equals ln e from Eq. (6)."},{"x":0.44162,"y":0.6271,"w":0.02453,"h":0.02013,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"lim hS0"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.65778,"w":0.36759,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"We now prove that e can be calculated as a certain limit."},{"x":0.35359,"y":0.70737,"w":0.53255,"h":0.02882,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"THEOREM 4—The Number e as a Limit The number e can be calculated as the limit"},{"x":0.58556,"y":0.74468,"w":0.09604,"h":0.02865,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"xS0(1 + x)1>x."},{"x":0.554,"y":0.75251,"w":0.05436,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"e = lim"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.79884,"w":0.58886,"h":0.02323,"fs":0.01311,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Proof If ƒ(x) = ln x, then ƒ′(x) = 1>x, so ƒ′(1) = 1. But, by the definition of derivative,"},{"x":0.15995,"y":0.81073,"w":0.07676,"h":0.01257,"fs":0.01023,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"y = (1 + x)1\u0004x"},{"x":0.4946,"y":0.83146,"w":0.11132,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"ƒ(1 + h) - ƒ(1)"},{"x":0.65647,"y":0.83146,"w":0.11038,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279